{"availability":"available","full":"cran/difNLR","name":"difNLR","description":":exclamation: This is a read-only mirror of the CRAN R package repository.  difNLR — DIF and DDF Detection by Non-Linear Regression Models  Report bugs for this package: https://github.com/adelahladka/difNLR/issues","category":"Other","language":"R","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2016-11-09T18:27:59Z","updated":"2025-11-19T15:35:17Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://shiny.cs.cas.cz/ShinyItemAnalysis/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:20.127Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:20.127Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:20.127Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.665Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T17:00:20.127Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DIF and DDF Detection by Non-Linear Regression Models.","The difNLR package provides methods for detecting differential item functioning (DIF) using non-linear regression models. Both uniform and non-uniform DIF effects can be detected when considering a single focal group. Additionally, the method allows for testing differences in guessing or inattention parameters between the reference and focal group. DIF detection is performed using either a likelihood-ratio test, an F-test, or Wald's test of a submodel. The software offers a variety of algorithms for estimating item parameters.","Furthermore, the difNLR package includes methods for detecting differential distractor functioning (DDF) using multinomial log-linear regression model. It also introduces DIF detection approaches for ordinal data via adjacent category logit and cumulative logit regression models."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cran/difNLR/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"92de53b26c252b14bc92c99db84e91e7ade893d26ab22c5ae3dce9267b5a262e","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.770Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.770Z","pro